import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>5.3b — Accessors &amp; Mutators: Getters with Guardrails</h1>

<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Basic Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Backpack with Limits</h3>
        <p>Yesterday you learned why accessor (getter) and mutator (setter) methods protect your data. Today you'll build an inventory system that uses mutators to enforce rules — no negative gold, no items over the weight limit.</p>
        <p>Create a class called <code>Backpack</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Private instance variables: <code>int gold</code>, <code>int currentWeight</code>, <code>int maxWeight</code></li>
            <li>Constructor takes <code>maxWeight</code>. Gold starts at 0, currentWeight at 0.</li>
            <li>Getter <code>getGold()</code>, getter <code>getCurrentWeight()</code>.</li>
            <li>Mutator <code>boolean addItem(int itemWeight)</code>: returns false if it would exceed maxWeight.</li>
            <li>Mutator <code>void addGold(int amount)</code>: refuses to add negative amounts. Print a warning if someone tries.</li>
            <li>Mutator <code>boolean spendGold(int amount)</code>: returns false if not enough gold.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Test Edge Cases</h3>
        <p>Create a Backpack(maxWeight=20). Try addItem(25) — should fail. Try addGold(-50) — should refuse. Try spendGold(100) when gold is 0 — should fail. Do all your guards work?</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-05/accessors-mutators.html">Accessors &amp; Mutators</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-03/boolean-logic.html">Booleans &amp; if Statements</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
